    "result_text": "The repo's test suite consists of the single `AcceptanceTest` (plus its `AcceptanceBase` helper), and it's green with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `initials` field on the Owner response.\n\n**Where the logic lives** \u2014 `Person` (the `@MappedSuperclass` holding `firstName`/`lastName`), since that's the single source of both names and this makes the derivation reusable for `Owner` and `Vet` alike:\n\n`src/main/java/.../model/Person.java`\n```java\n@Transient\npublic String getInitials() {\n    return initial(this.firstName) + initial(this.lastName);\n}\n\nprivate static String initial(String name) {\n    return name.substring(0, 1).toUpperCase(Locale.ROOT) + \".\";\n}\n```\n`getInitials()` produces `\"J.S.\"` \u2014 each name's upper-cased first letter followed by a dot. `@Transient` keeps it out of JPA persistence (it's derived, not a column).\n\n**Exposing it on the DTO** \u2014 added an `initials` read-only property to the `Owner` schema in `src/main/resources/openapi.yml`, mirroring the existing `displayName`. The generated `OwnerDto` then gains `getInitials`/`setInitials`, and MapStruct's `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto` auto-maps it from `owner.getInitials()` by name \u2014 no extra `@Mapping` or responder changes needed.\n\nThe `coreComputesInitials` acceptance test (firstName `\"john\"`, lastName `\"smith\"` \u2192 `$.initials == \"J.S.\"`) passes, and the full suite builds green.",
